<title>GERMANY: Bundesbank sets 14-day repo tender at 3 pct rate.</title>
<headline>Bundesbank sets 14-day repo tender at 3 pct rate.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bundesbank said on Tuesday it was setting a tender for 14-day securities repurchase funds, offering banks liquidity at a fixed three percent rate.</p>
<p>Funds will be credited to accounts tomorrow and the securities have to be repurchased on Oct 23.</p>
<p>A 67.8 billion mark facility set at a fixed three percent rate expires on Wednesday. The repo rates has been fixed at three percent since late August.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
